<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Lachish</h1><p class="st-meta">1800 BCE – 1150 BCE (approx.) · capital Lachish</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Lachish, a major Canaanite city of the Shephelah lowlands and Egyptian vassal in the Amarna age, later the second city of Judah.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Lachish, at Tel Lachish west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebron">Hebron</a>, became a large fortified city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-bronze-age">Middle Bronze Age</a>, protected by a steep glacis. It controlled the fertile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shephelah">Shephelah</a> between the coastal plain and the Judaean hills and the roads leading to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age">Late Bronze Age</a> its kings, including Zimreddi and Shipti-Ba'lu, were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/egyptian-empire-new-kingdom">Egyptian Empire New Kingdom</a> and wrote to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amarna-letters">Amarna letters</a>. Excavations revealed a temple in the old moat, the Fosse Temple, and inscriptions in early alphabetic script.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Canaanite city was destroyed and abandoned in the 12th century BCE, probably during the collapse of Egyptian rule. Rebuilt in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a>, it became a fortress of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-judah">Kingdom of Judah</a>, famously besieged by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sennacherib">Sennacherib</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> in 701 BCE.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lachish.jpg" alt="Lachish" width="320" height="234"><figcaption>Image: Wilson44691 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LachishFrontGate.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1800 BCE – 1150 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century-bce">19th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century-bce">12th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lachish</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Zimreddi, Shipti-Ba'lu</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Canaanite religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Canaanite, Akkadian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/israel">Israel</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Canaanite Lachish</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1475&amp;focus=lachish" aria-label="Lachish on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5579 1028 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lachish lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5899 1284L5863 1489"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5863 1489h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5899 1284h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5899 1284h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=-1475&amp;focus=lachish">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

